#uuid "29164807-d381-53a4-8efb-e16c83f907bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-140515" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(C-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3-\\lambda  \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda )+(-\\lambda -5)-(5+\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+15\\lambda )-\\lambda -5-5-\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+13\\lambda -10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08b84ff5-4873-5847-ad69-723f5136d9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321215} {:answer/id #uuid "3ddd2395-53d8-54c0-bd86-c597005e66e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321632} {:answer/id #uuid "99197694-172f-58f3-819b-f3608767e4ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322363} {:answer/id #uuid "d34c4ee0-a109-57af-bb18-6dbdec953f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322798} {:answer/id #uuid "dca8a51f-11ad-5fb9-a502-863404f1d921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dca8a51f-11ad-5fb9-a502-863404f1d921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322872} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1deec07-22ce-59a9-8917-9f15fef7cfa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c699a77c-6393-5572-b010-6743d9f3bb17" :question/math-academy-id "q-37355" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\lambda =-1$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- $\\lambda =-10$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- The eigenvalue $\\lambda =-10$ has algebraic multiplicity $3$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $2$nd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-10-\\lambda )\\cdot (-10-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ -18 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )^{2}((-1-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )-54) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{2}({\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda -50) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{2}(\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{3}(\\lambda -5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda =-10$ (with algebraic multiplicity $3$) and $\\lambda =5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124523 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c92bdd9-561f-50f8-a0af-b026acb7e7d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -52=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321751} {:answer/id #uuid "679f1b6a-bb22-58ad-9008-20f76acaf14c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-10{\\lambda }^{2}+43\\lambda -90=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321955} {:answer/id #uuid "688684d9-f540-59a5-826c-2faac539f6c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+7{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -48=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321961} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e445b9-3e7b-5df5-8de9-a07b0a91fd34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045